          dealing: "Player to dealer's right cuts and forms two 11-card piles (mortos) set aside. Dealer deals 11 cards to each player from remaining pack. Remaining 42 cards form draw pile (monte). Discard pile (lixo/bagaÃ§o) starts empty.",
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Be the first team to reach 3000 points by melding sequences, creating canastas (7+ card sequences), and going out. Score points from melded cards plus bonuses for canastas.',
          gameplay: "First player (to dealer's right) draws top card, decides to keep or discard it, then may meld and must discard. Play proceeds counter-clockwise. Each turn: draw from stock or take entire discard pile; optionally meld or add to team melds; discard one card. First player to empty hand takes a morto (11-card extra hand). Second morto goes to first player of other team who runs out. Team can end play with second batida if they have a clean canastra (7+ cards without wild).",
          keyRules: [
            '108 cards: 2 decks + 4 jokers; twos are wild',
            'Two 11-card mortos set aside for first players out',
            'Melds are sequences of 3+ consecutive cards of a suit',
            'Aces rank high and low: A-2-3-...-Q-K-A possible',
            'Max one wild card per sequence',
            'Canastra = sequence of 7+ cards (clean or dirty)',
            'Need clean canastra to go out',
            'Target: 3000 points',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Prioritize creating your first canastra early. Save wild cards (jokers and twos) for completing sequences. Watch which cards your partner is collecting. Take the discard pile only when it helps complete valuable melds.',
          intermediate: 'Track which cards have been played to predict what opponents hold. Coordinate with partner on which sequences to build. Time your batida carefully - taking a morto gives more cards but may help opponents. Consider vulnerability status when planning initial melds.',
          advanced: 'Calculate risk vs reward when taking the discard pile (opponents see what you take). Manage wild cards strategically - they complete sequences but reduce canastra value. Force opponents to take mortos at disadvantageous times. In endgame, block opponents from completing canastras while setting up your own go-out.',
          tips: [
            'Always try to create at least one clean canastra for going out',
            'Save wild cards for critical sequence completions',
            "Watch partner's discards to understand their hand",
            'Taking a morto after discarding (batida indireta) delays using it',
            'Going out quickly can deny opponents their morto bonus',
            'Vulnerable teams need 75+ points for first meld',
            'A canastra real (14-card clean sequence) scores 1000 bonus points',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
